From: PikuZheng <cba321123@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:43:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): touch connection on EPOLLIN to prevent 32KB buffer leak on timeout
Origin: https://github.com/PikuZheng/smartdns/commit/6e99ff706f246dc1af3fec34955db49139ce714b
Upstream-Status: Backported from downstream PikuZheng/canary

_dns_server_process missed touching conn on event dispatch, which caused
32KB buffer residue on each connection closed by timeout. Over days of operation,
this accumulated as a slow but fatal memory leak on embedded routers.
---
diff --git a/src/dns_server/dns_server.c b/src/dns_server/dns_server.c
index 5378bdee..b5f5ea70 100644
--- a/src/dns_server/dns_server.c
+++ b/src/dns_server/dns_server.c
@@ -572,7 +572,9 @@ errout:
 static int _dns_server_process(struct dns_server_conn_head *conn, struct epoll_event *event, unsigned long now)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
-	_dns_server_client_touch(conn);
+	if (event->events & EPOLLIN) {
+		_dns_server_client_touch(conn);
+	}
 	_dns_server_conn_get(conn);
 	if (conn->type == DNS_CONN_TYPE_UDP_SERVER) {
 		struct dns_server_conn_udp *udpconn = (struct dns_server_conn_udp *)conn;
-- 
2.54.0.windows.1

